  "id": "COMPOUND:15828 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Nardosinanol G appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step pathway that ultimately targets Neuropilin-2. The evidence suggests that Nardosinanol G directly interacts with CDK2/Cyclin A1, which is a key regulator of the cell cycle. This interaction is further mediated by (1S,8R,11R)-3,3,7,11-tetramethyl-12-oxatricyclo[6.3.1.01,5]dodeca-4,6-dien-8-ol, a compound that is also a target of Nardosinanol G. This compound, in turn, influences Neuropilin-2, indicating a potential role in cellular processes involving proliferation and signaling. The presence of multiple targets along this pathway suggests that Nardosinanol G may act as a modulator of cellular functions through a complex network of molecular interactions. The integration of these targets highlights the importance of CDK2/Cyclin A1 in the downstream effects of Nardosinanol G, with Neuropilin-2 being a critical downstream effector in this cascade.",
